{"content_hash": "6d69edc7695c7c10", "version_id": 430, "article_id": 43, "level_code": "ja_n1", "lang": "ja", "level": 5, "level_label": "N1 上級", "title": "NHS待機リストが2カ月連続増 冬の圧力に「不吉な兆候」", "title_zh": "NHS等候名单连续两月增加，冬季压力出现“不祥征兆”", "has_translation": true, "topic": "health", "source": "bbc_health", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxnv03e9nmp4o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540683153640-c28d7f6810f0?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8N3x8b21pbm91cyUyMHNpZ25zJTIwd2ludGVyfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ0Mzd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Shawn Bagley on Unsplash", "author": "Shawn Bagley", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@utahdesertguy?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/road-sign-near-pine-trees-bUADDFi1Qs0?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(352, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(30, 46%, 48%)", "label": "HEALTH", "seed": "b128cdf1738d"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 310, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "イングランドのNHSで、日常的な病院治療を待つ患者数が2カ月連続で増加した。医療指導者らは、冬の圧力がすでに現場を襲い始めていると警告し、政府が掲げる2029年までの目標達成に疑問を投げかけている。", "lead_zh": "英格兰NHS等待常规医院治疗的患者人数连续两个月增加。医疗负责人警告，冬季压力已经开始冲击一线，并对政府提出的到2029年实现的目标提出质疑。", "preview": "イングランドのNHSでは、8月末時点で約737万件の治療が待機しており、これは624万人の患者に相当する。2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるかどうかが問われている。待機リストの増加は、NHSが夏の", "preview_zh": "英格兰NHS截至8月底约有737万件治疗等待进行，涉及624万名患者。这是自2025年10月以来的最高水平，也让政府能否在2029年前实现92%的患者在18周内得到治疗的目标受到质疑。等待名单增加之际，NHS在夏季提供了创纪录的计划性医疗，需求也达到历史最高。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 420, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/43/ja_n1.mp3", "duration": 70.263, "size_bytes": 425376, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 217, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/430.json", "paragraphs": ["イングランドのNHSでは、8月末時点で約737万件の治療が待機しており、これは624万人の患者に相当する。2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるかどうかが問われている。待機リストの増加は、NHSが夏の間に記録的な計画医療を提供したにもかかわらず生じており、需要も過去最高に達した。", "6月から8月にかけては、過去最多となる470万件の計画治療・処置・予約が実施された。しかし、9月には救急部門と救急車サービスがともに記録的な患者数に直面した。NHSイングランドのフランキー・ソーズ医学部長は、最前線のチームの進歩にもかかわらず、冬の圧力がすでに高まっていると警告し、「スタッフはすでに不吉な初期兆候を目にしている」と述べた。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["英格兰NHS截至8月底约有737万件治疗等待进行，涉及624万名患者。这是自2025年10月以来的最高水平，也让政府能否在2029年前实现92%的患者在18周内得到治疗的目标受到质疑。等待名单增加之际，NHS在夏季提供了创纪录的计划性医疗，需求也达到历史最高。", "6月至8月期间，共实施了创纪录的470万件计划治疗、手术和预约。但9月，急诊科和救护车服务都面临创纪录的患者数量。NHS英格兰首席医务官弗兰基·索兹警告说，尽管一线团队取得进展，冬季压力已经在积聚，并称“员工已经看到不祥的早期迹象”。"], "body": "イングランドのNHSでは、8月末時点で約737万件の治療が待機しており、これは624万人の患者に相当する。2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるかどうかが問われている。待機リストの増加は、NHSが夏の間に記録的な計画医療を提供したにもかかわらず生じており、需要も過去最高に達した。\n\n6月から8月にかけては、過去最多となる470万件の計画治療・処置・予約が実施された。しかし、9月には救急部門と救急車サービスがともに記録的な患者数に直面した。NHSイングランドのフランキー・ソーズ医学部長は、最前線のチームの進歩にもかかわらず、冬の圧力がすでに高まっていると警告し、「スタッフはすでに不吉な初期兆候を目にしている」と述べた。", "body_zh": "英格兰NHS截至8月底约有737万件治疗等待进行，涉及624万名患者。这是自2025年10月以来的最高水平，也让政府能否在2029年前实现92%的患者在18周内得到治疗的目标受到质疑。等待名单增加之际，NHS在夏季提供了创纪录的计划性医疗，需求也达到历史最高。\n\n6月至8月期间，共实施了创纪录的470万件计划治疗、手术和预约。但9月，急诊科和救护车服务都面临创纪录的患者数量。NHS英格兰首席医务官弗兰基·索兹警告说，尽管一线团队取得进展，冬季压力已经在积聚，并称“员工已经看到不祥的早期迹象”。", "text": "イングランドのNHSでは、8月末時点で約737万件の治療が待機しており、これは624万人の患者に相当する。2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるかどうかが問われている。待機リストの増加は、NHSが夏の間に記録的な計画医療を提供したにもかかわらず生じており、需要も過去最高に達した。 6月から8月にかけては、過去最多となる470万件の計画治療・処置・予約が実施された。しかし、9月には救急部門と救急車サービスがともに記録的な患者数に直面した。NHSイングランドのフランキー・ソーズ医学部長は、最前線のチームの進歩にもかかわらず、冬の圧力がすでに高まっていると警告し、「スタッフはすでに不吉な初期兆候を目にしている」と述べた。", "vocab": [{"word": "待機リスト", "pos": "noun", "zh": "等候名单", "note": "医疗语境中常指手术或治疗等待名单"}, {"word": "不吉な兆候", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "不祥征兆", "note": "用于预示不好事情即将发生的迹象"}, {"word": "記録的な", "pos": "adj", "zh": "创纪录的", "note": "形容达到历史最高水平"}, {"word": "計画医療", "pos": "noun", "zh": "计划性医疗", "note": "指非紧急的择期治疗"}, {"word": "救急部門", "pos": "noun", "zh": "急诊科", "note": "医院接收紧急患者的部门"}, {"word": "絶え間ない", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不断的、持续不停的", "note": "常与增长、努力等词搭配"}, {"word": "停滞", "pos": "noun", "zh": "停滞", "note": "表示没有进展或停止不前"}, {"word": "紹介件数", "pos": "noun", "zh": "转诊数量", "note": "医疗中由医生推荐到专科的数量"}, {"word": "警鐘を鳴らす", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "敲响警钟", "note": "惯用表达，提醒危险或问题"}, {"word": "前年比", "pos": "noun", "zh": "同比", "note": "与去年同期相比"}, {"word": "懸念の種", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "担忧的根源", "note": "引起担心的事情"}, {"word": "最前線", "pos": "noun", "zh": "一线、最前线", "note": "指直接面对患者或问题的现场"}, {"word": "公約", "pos": "noun", "zh": "竞选承诺、公开承诺", "note": "政治语境中常指政府许下的诺言"}, {"word": "達成", "pos": "noun", "zh": "达成、实现", "note": "常用于目标、指标等"}, {"word": "負担", "pos": "noun", "zh": "负担", "note": "可指工作压力或医疗系统承受的压力"}, {"word": "投資", "pos": "noun", "zh": "投资", "note": "此处指政府对医疗设施投入资金"}], "title_original": "'Ominous signs' of winter pressures as NHS waiting list grows", "summary_original": "NHS winter pressures appear to be building already, with rises in waiting times for planned surgery.", "body_original": "'Ominous signs' of winter pressures as NHS waiting list grows\nBy\nDominic Hughes\nHealth correspondent\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nThere are \"ominous signs\" that winter pressures are already affecting the NHS in England, according to senior health leaders.\nThe warning comes as new data reveals the waiting list for routine hospital treatment in England rose for the second month in a row.\nAn estimated 7.37 million treatments were waiting to be carried out at the end of August, relating to 6.24 million patients.\nThe numbers are the highest since October 2025 and have raised questions over whether the NHS will meet a government target of treating 92% of patients within 18 weeks by 2029.\nThe rise in waiting lists comes despite the NHS in England delivering what were described as record levels of planned, elective care over the summer, while demand for services also reached its highest level ever.\nA record 4.7 million planned treatments, procedures and appointments occurred across June, July and August – more than in any previous summer.\nBut both A&Es and ambulance services also saw a record number of patients for the month of September.\nNHS England's national medical director, Professor Frankie Swords, warned that despite the progress delivered by frontline teams, winter pressure was already building.\n\"Staff are already seeing the ominous early signs of pressure, with more patients coming to A&E with flu and other respiratory viruses than usual for this time of year, and unfortunately many people are still waiting longer than we would like them to,\" she said.\nHealth and Social Care Secretary, Yvette Cooper said the NHS has been dealing with summer pressures as well as winter pressures.\n\"It is a huge tribute to doctors, nurses and staff across the NHS that alongside dealing with unprecedented levels of A&E attendances and ambulance call-outs, they also managed to deliver record numbers of elective appointments, procedures and treatments.\n\"Step by step, our NHS has been increasing its delivery and performance, making a real difference to patients' lives even as demand is growing.\n\"But with winter now approaching, pressure on our NHS is set to increase again and I would encourage everyone who is eligible for the flu jab and other vaccines to get themselves protected against preventable illnesses, and help relieve the workload on the NHS too.\"\n\"Relentless growth in demand for care\"\nThe NHS Alliance, which represents hospitals, says the government in England is not going to achieve its manifesto promise of hitting the 18-week hospital waiting time target by the end of the parliament in 2029.\nThat 18-week target hasn't been hit for a decade.\nA separate analysis by the Health Foundation think-tank said progress on cutting waiting times had stalled over the past year, with referrals on to the waiting list rising at a much quicker rate than the number of patients being treated.\nSir Ciarán Devane, the chief executive of the NHS Alliance which represents NHS trusts, said: \"The NHS continues to respond to record demand for care, but the relentless growth in demand for services is putting NHS staff under real pressure.\"\nFrancesca Cavallaro, of the Health Foundation, said: \"Thanks to the hard work of staff, the NHS has made progress in bringing down waiting times, but a rise in referrals mean that the service is having to run faster just to stand still and the prospects of meeting the government's pledge are receding.\n\"Andy Burnham's government have yet to set out whether they will give the 18-week target the same priority as it had under Keir Starmer, but our analysis shows the pledge is becoming increasingly hard to deliver.\"\n\"Not just numbers, but vulnerable people\"\nThere will be concern too that the pressures of a long, hot summer have merged almost seamlessly into the pressures associated with the winter months.\nMore patients, including children, have been arriving at A&E departments with flu and other respiratory viruses.\nThe number of patients seen within four hours in A&Es last month fell to 74.4%, down from 75.0% in August.\nThe number of people waiting more than 12 hours in A&E departments from a decision to admit to actually being admitted – what is known as \"corridor care\" – stood at 50,582 in September, up from 44,951 in August.\nThat has alarmed Dr Vicky Price, president of the Society for Acute Medicine.\n\"A 13% year-on-year rise in 12-hour emergency department waits as winter approaches should set alarm bells ringing.\n\"More than 50,000 patients waited over 12 hours from the decision to admit to admission in September - 1,686 people every day.\n\"These are not just numbers.\n\"They represent vulnerable people who are waiting far too long for a bed and staff trying to deliver safe care in overcrowded emergency departments.\"\nThe government says the 18-week mark could still be achieved, saying it was investing in NHS buildings and equipment to make services more productive.\nIt also pointed to disruption to care that was caused by the strikes by resident doctors, a dispute which has now been settled.\nBut the strain that services are feeling in September, before winter has even really got going, will be a cause for concern among NHS leaders and their political bosses alike.\nGet in touch\nHave you been on an NHS waiting list for a long time? Share your experience\nContact form\nContact form\nRelated topics\nNHS\nEngland\nHealth\nNHS England\nWaiting times\nMore on this story\nRise in people waiting for NHS treatment for fourth month in a row\nPublished\n17 September\nFears of two-tier health system as more turn to private care, says watchdog\nPublished\n16 March\nI'm on six different NHS waiting lists - it's taking over my life\nPublished\n23 April", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:07:16.505883", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "イングランド", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.775, "sm": 125, "em": 775, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.787, "e": 0.912, "sm": 787, "em": 912, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "NHS", "s": 0.925, "e": 1.775, "sm": 925, "em": 1775, "cs": 7, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "で", "s": 1.788, "e": 1.9, "sm": 1787, "em": 1900, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "は", "s": 1.913, "e": 2.15, "sm": 1912, "em": 2150, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "、", "s": 2.15, "e": 2.337, "sm": 2150, "em": 2337, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "8", "s": 2.337, "e": 2.612, "sm": 2337, "em": 2612, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "月", "s": 2.612, "e": 2.888, "sm": 2612, "em": 2887, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "末", "s": 2.9, "e": 3.15, "sm": 2900, "em": 3150, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "時点", "s": 3.163, "e": 3.513, "sm": 3162, "em": 3512, "cs": 16, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "で", "s": 3.525, "e": 3.625, "sm": 3525, "em": 3625, "cs": 18, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i